>> title: Beef Stroganoff
>> category: Noodles
>> tags: beef, mushrooms, egg noodles, sour cream, one-pot, skillet
>> counters: One Pot
>> aka: stroganoff, beef stroganov, bef stroganov, beef and noodles in sour cream
>> servings: 4
>> time: 45 min
>> slack: narrow — sour cream splits if it boils, so the pan comes off the heat and stops moving before it goes in, and a split sauce does not come back; loosen it with hot water rather than putting it back on the burner
>> step.1: The noodles cook in the beef's own broth in the same pan, which is the version worth writing down: the usual one boils them in a second pot and drains them, and then the dish is two pots and a colander. Sear the beef first, take it out to a plate, and it goes back in at the very end.
>> step.2: sear 3 min, out to a plate
>> step.3: brown 8 min
>> step.4: stir in the flour, 1 min
>> step.5: simmer 12 min, noodles take up the liquid
>> step.6: fold in off the heat, beef back
>> step.7: Sour cream splits if it boils, so the pan comes off the heat and stops moving before it goes in. If the sauce looks tight after the fold, loosen it with a spoonful of hot water rather than putting it back on the burner.

The noodles cook in the beef's own broth in the same pan, which is the version worth writing down: the usual one boils them in a second pot and drains them, and then the dish is two pots and a colander. Sear the beef first, take it out to a plate, and it goes back in at the very end.

Sear @beef sirloin{1 1/4%lb}(570 g; cut in thin strips), @kosher salt{1 1/2%tsp} in @unsalted butter{1%Tbs} in a #large skillet{} for ~sear{3%min}, then out to a plate.

Brown @cremini mushrooms{12%oz}(340 g; sliced thick), @yellow onion{1%large}(sliced) in @unsalted butter{2%Tbs} for ~brown{8%min}.

Stir @&(~1)mushrooms{} with @all-purpose flour{2%Tbs}(16 g), @sweet paprika{2%tsp}, @Dijon mustard{1%Tbs} for ~stir{1%min}.

Simmer @&(~1)pan{} with @beef stock{3%cups}(710 mL), @wide egg noodles{8%oz}(225 g) for ~simmer{12%min}, stirring, until the noodles are tender and the liquid has gone into them.

Fold @&(~4)seared beef{}, @sour cream{3/4%cup}(180 g), @dill{2%Tbs}(chopped), @black pepper{1/2%tsp} into @&(~1)noodles{} off the heat.

Sour cream splits if it boils, so the pan comes off the heat and stops moving before it goes in. If the sauce looks tight after the fold, loosen it with a spoonful of hot water rather than putting it back on the burner.
